        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm analyzing अमोटिष्म as luṅ kartari uttama bahuvacana from root मुट्, trying to place it in the right gaṇa — checking whether मुट् आक्षेपमर्दनयोः belongs to तुदादि or another class.\n\nActually, मुट in the कुटादि subgroup of तुदादि takes ङित् iṭ-affixes, meaning no guṇa, which would give अमुटिष्म rather than अमोटिष्म. That mismatch makes me consider whether this form comes from a भ्वादि or चुरादि मुट्/मुड् instead, which would permit guṇa.\n\nFor curādi, luṅ would give अमूमुटाम via caṅ, so अमोटिष्म points more toward bhvādi or tudādi without kuṭādi, since seṭ iṭ in luṅ isn't ṅit and guṇa occurs there too, giving ambiguity between the two classes. I'm trying to recall whether मुट belongs to the कुटादि gaṇa, checking through the list of roots like कुट, पुट, कुच, गुज, गुड, डिप, छुर to see if it's included.\n\nI'm trying to pin down whether अमोटिष्म belongs to the tudādi मुट or a separate bhvādi root like मुड/पुड meaning \"to crush\" — checking the Dhatupatha entries to see which root actually fits this luṅ form.\n\nSo taking मुट as bhvādi, the laṅ form would be अमोटाम. I'll go with अमोटाम as the answer.\n\n",
        "signature": ""
      },
